  "title": "Mansa Musa",
  "summary": "Mansa Musa ruled the Mali Empire from 1312 to 1337, according to World History Encyclopedia. In 1324 he set out on pilgrimage to Mecca, reaching Cairo in July for a three-month stay. Accounts say his spending there lowered the gold dinar's value by about 20 percent. He also had mosques built at Gao and Timbuktu.",
